 "Custom RC Car": "自制遥控车",
 "In high school I designed and built a four-wheel-drive, tank-steer RC car from discrete components and controlled it from my phone. An Arduino Uno decodes gamepad commands from the Dabble app over a Bluetooth serial link and drives four DC gear motors through an L298N dual H-bridge, with PWM speed control and ramped acceleration in firmware, all powered by two parallel 9 V batteries behind a master isolation switch. I modelled the chassis, motor mounts, and removable body shell in Autodesk Fusion and fabricated them by FDM 3D printing.": "高中时，我用分立元件设计并制作了一辆四轮驱动、坦克式转向的遥控车，并用手机控制它。Arduino Uno 通过蓝牙串口接收 Dabble 应用发出的手柄指令并解码，经由 L298N 双 H 桥驱动四个直流减速电机，固件中实现了 PWM 调速和渐进加速；整车由两节并联的 9 V 电池供电，并配有总隔离开关。我在 Autodesk Fusion 中建模了底盘、电机支架和可拆卸车壳，并用 FDM 3D 打印制作。",
 "L298N Motor Controllers": "L298N 电机驱动器",
