 "Ultrasonic Light-Up Drawer": "超声波感应灯抽屉",
 "This is a 3D printed drawer that illuminates itself automatically when opened. An HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor mounted in the housing measures the drawer's displacement by time-of-flight ranging, and an Arduino applies a median filter and hysteresis thresholds to that signal before fading an LED on through PWM once the drawer passes a set distance, and off again when it closes. I designed the drawer and housing in Autodesk Fusion and wrote the firmware. It was my first complete embedded system, from sensor acquisition to actuated output.": "这是一个 3D 打印的抽屉，打开时会自动亮灯。安装在外壳中的 HC-SR04 超声波传感器通过飞行时间测距来测量抽屉的位移，Arduino 对该信号进行中值滤波并设置迟滞阈值，当抽屉拉出超过设定距离时，通过 PWM 让 LED 渐亮，关上时再渐灭。抽屉和外壳由我在 Autodesk Fusion 中设计，固件也由我编写。这是我第一个完整的嵌入式系统，从传感器采集到执行输出一应俱全。",
